          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a
            %strong formal dg-algebra
            if it is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasiisomorphism"} quasi-isomorphic
            (i.e.:
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            of the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras"} model structure on dg-algebras
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≃
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A
                  \\xrightarrow{\;\;\; \simeq \;\;\;}
                  H^\bullet(A)
          %p
            to its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology+and+cohomology"} chain (co)homology
            regarded as a dg-algebra with trivial differential.
          %p
            Since all dg-algebras are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+object"} fibrant
            in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras"} standard model structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
          #eq:TheSpan.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi w
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Q
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≃
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A
                  \\overset{\;\; \simeq_w \;\;}{\leftarrow}
                  Q A
                  \\overset{\;\; \simeq \;\;}{\rightarrow}
                  H^\bullet(A)
          %p
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
            of dg-algebras.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+topological+spaces"} rational topological spaces
            are encoded in their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+algebra"} Sullivan dg-algebras
            (cf. The
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+theorem+of+dg-algebraic+rational+homotopy+theory"} fundamental theorem of dg-algebraic rational homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            whose Sullivan dg-algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(X)
            is formal is called a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong formal topological space
            = succeed "," do
              %strong formal rational space
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+topology"} formal topology
            = succeed "." do
              %strong formal homotopy type
          %p Examples:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                compact
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} Kähler manifolds
                (e.g. smooth projective varieties),
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groups"}> Lie groups
                ,
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+spaces"} classifying spaces
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;B G
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groups"} Lie groups
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %li
              %p
                some
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homogeneous+spaces"} homogeneous spaces
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
                (see (
                %a{:href => "#Amann12"}> Amann 12
                ) for
                = succeed "formal" do
                  %em non
            %li
              %p
                the unstable
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spaces"} Thom spaces
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M U_n
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mi S
                        %msub
                          %mi O
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M S O_n
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+space"} Eilenberg-MacLane space
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\mathbb{Z},n)
              %p
                whose Sullivan minimal model is the dg-algebra on a single degree
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo =
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} =n
                generator with trivial differential.,
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/the+little+n-disk+operad+is+formal"}> the little n-disk operad is formal
                \.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-cohomology"} H-cohomology
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Early discussion of formal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+model"} Sullivan model
            dg-algebras in the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
          %ul
            %li#Sullivan77
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dennis+Sullivan"}> Dennis Sullivan
                , section 12 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Infinitesimal computations in topology
                %strong 47
                (1977) 269-331 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=PMIHES_1977__47__269_0"}> numdam:PMIHES_1977__47__269_0
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://archive.numdam.org/article/PMIHES_1977__47__269_0.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"}> Pierre Deligne
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Phillip+Griffiths"} Phillip Griffiths
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Morgan"} John Morgan
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dennis+Sullivan"} Dennis Sullivan
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Real homotopy theory of Kähler manifolds
                %strong 29
                (1975) 245-274 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01389853"}> doi:10.1007/BF01389853
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Since
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+models"} Sullivan models
            are also
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TheSpan"} (1)
          %ul
            %li#Hess06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kathryn+Hess"}> Kathryn Hess
                , Def. 2.1 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Rational homotopy theory: a brief introduction
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://jdc.math.uwo.ca/summerschool/"} Summer School on Interactions between Homotopy Theory and Algebra
                = succeed "&rbrack;," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0604626"} arXiv:math.AT/0604626
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Christensen"} Dan Christensen
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"} William Dwyer
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Mandell"} Michael Mandell
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
                (eds.),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Interactions between Homotopy Theory and Algebra
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 436
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1090/conm/436"} doi:10.1090/conm/436
            %li{:id => "Aambø21"}
              %p
                Torgeir Aambø, Def. 1.15 &amp; Theorem A (p.2):
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On formal DG-algebras
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://hdl.handle.net/11250/2778399"} hndl:11250/2778399
          %p
            Review with an eye towards the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dd%5Ec-lemma"} dd^c-lemma
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-cohomology"} H-cohomology
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Cavalcanti03
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gil+Cavalcanti"}> Gil Cavalcanti
              , p. 12 of
              %em
                New aspects of the
                = succeed "-lemma" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %msup
                          %mi d
                          %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d d^c
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0501406"}> arXiv:math/0501406
              )
          %p
            The case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+algebras"} Sullivan algebras
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+bundles"} sphere bundles
          %ul
            %li
              Jiawei Zhou,
              %em Formality of Sphere Bundles
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.09594"}> arXiv:2304.09594
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p A construction of nonformal homogeneous spaces:
          %ul
            %li#Amann12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Manuel+Amann"}> Manuel Amann
              \.
              %em Non-formal Homogeneous Spaces
              (2012). (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1206.0786"}> arXiv:1206.0786
              ).
